over the years Greek mythology has given  us a host of monsters and creatures  along with their origin stories but one  of the lesser well-known stories is that  of King Lycaon and the legend of the  first werewolf Lycaon was the son of  Peleus one of the first mortals to walk  on earth there are quite a few variant  accounts on how Pulaski scam to exist  some believe he was born of the soil and  others believed that he was one of the  first mortal sons of Zeus like haein  would succeed his father and become the  king of the region that we now refer to  as Arcadia over time he had become very  famous because of his vast array of  wives two of which even included NIMS  naturally with so many wives came an  abundance of children it's generally  believed that Lycaon was father to over  50 sons the exact number of sons does  tend to vary depending on the source  material like haiyan's sons would travel  across the kingdom found in many of the  cities in Arcadia the downfall of lycaon  is a well-documented event that is quite  often split into several different  stories one of the stories told depicts  like Cain as a righteous king who  established his own City and even named  the mountain after himself he was  particularly fond of the Lycaon games  and he even constructed a temple in the  name of Zeus to honor him during the  games  it was the method that Lycaon used in  his worship of Zeus that was most  disturbing he would often sacrifice a  child upon the altar of Zeus the act of  human sacrifice especially that of a  child was something that Zeus would not  tolerate and as a result he rained down  bolts of lightning killing Lycaon and  his sons the more commonly told story is  what many believed to be the origin of  the werewolf legend in this version like  Cain was seen as a mischievous and  slightly deceitful king  in order to test Lycaon Zeus disguised  himself as a common laborer and visited  his kingdom so he could judge firsthand  what type of King like haein was as zeus  wandered through the kingdom his  divinity started to become apparent and  people began worshipping the stranger  like haein unaware of which deity it was  visiting his kingdom decided that he  would test the stranger he arranged for  a large banquet that he invited the  stranger to he then sacrificed the child  whose body pots were boiled and roasted  in preparation for the main course in  some cases it was a random child that  was sacrificed and in other versions it  was one of like haiyan's own sons when  the meal was served zeus revealed his  true identity and in his anger he  overturned the table and just as in the  last story zu struck down like a n' and  his sons now there are a handful of  different ways that this story ends some  believed that zeus only struck down like  haiyan's children and whilst this was  happening he attempted to flee zeus then  transformed him into a half wolf half  human creature and thus the legend of  the werewolf began the son that like  Haiyan had sacrificed Nick Thomas the  youngest of all of his sons was  resurrected by the gods and in most  cases he would become like a and  successor and the new king of Arcadia  the story of lycaon is quite an  intriguing tale  unlike most kings and mortals he did not  seem to fear the gods and this could be  partly to do with the fact that he  believes himself to be above mortals and  even a God of sorts himself it was this  disregard that led him to believe that  he could feed a god one of his own  children with no repercussions  ultimately his actions led to him being  cursed if he was to act like an animal  then in turn he will become one  hopefully you guys enjoyed the story if  you did let me know what you thought in  the comments below if werewolves are  something that interest you then I do  have an in-depth video on the origins of  the werewolf legend and how its evolved  over the years  there'll be an end screen that you guys  can click on and I'll leave a link in  the description but as always I've been  your host mythology in fiction explained
 

